## Quick Start (Copy-Paste Commands)

# Install mcp-server-github
uv tool install mcp-server-github

# Apply chezmoi configuration (generates ~/.config/claude-code/mcp.json)
chezmoi apply --refresh-externals=never

# Verify installation
claude mcp list

## Prerequisites

# Install uv (for MCP integration)
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh

# Create GitHub Personal Access Token
# 1. Go to: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# 2. Click "Generate new token" (classic)
# 3. Select scopes: repo, read:org (adjust based on needs)
# 4. Copy the token (starts with ghp_)
# 5. Add it to your chezmoi data file (see Configuration section below)

## Installation

# Install mcp-server-github using uv
uv tool install mcp-server-github

## Configuration with Chezmoi

# The GitHub MCP server is configured via chezmoi template:
# File: ~/.local/share/chezmoi/dot_config/claude-code/mcp.json.tmpl

# Template content:
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "mcp-server-github",
      "args": [],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "{{ .github_token }}"
      }
    }
  }
}

# The {{ .github_token }} variable should be defined in your chezmoi data file:
# - ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml (TOML format)
# - ~/.local/share/chezmoi/.chezmoidata.yaml (YAML format)

# Example chezmoi.toml:
[data]
  github_token = "ghp_your_token_here"

# Example .chezmoidata.yaml:
github_token: "ghp_your_token_here"

## Applying Configuration

# Apply chezmoi configuration (skip externals to avoid API issues)
chezmoi apply --refresh-externals=never

# Or apply specific file only
chezmoi apply ~/.config/claude-code/mcp.json

## Verification

# Verify MCP server is configured
claude mcp list

# Should show:
# github: mcp-server-github - ✓ Connected

# List available MCP resources
claude mcp resources --server github

## Available MCP Tools

The GitHub MCP server provides tools for:
- Repository management (create, read, update repos)
- Issue tracking (create, list, update issues)
- Pull request operations (create, review, merge PRs)
- File operations (read, write files in repos)
- Search (search code, issues, PRs)

