## Troubleshooting

# Check if mcp-server-github is installed
which mcp-server-github

# Test the token manually
curl -H "Authorization: token {{ .github_token }}" https://api.github.com/user

# Check chezmoi data
chezmoi data | grep github_token

# Re-apply configuration
chezmoi apply --refresh-externals=never ~/.config/claude-code/mcp.json

# Check Claude MCP status
claude mcp list --verbose

## Security Notes

- Never commit your GitHub token to version control
- Use chezmoi's encryption features for sensitive data:
  - chezmoi can encrypt files with age or gpg
  - Consider using `encrypted_` prefix for sensitive templates
- Rotate tokens periodically
- Use fine-grained tokens with minimal required scopes

## Alternative: Manual Configuration

# If not using chezmoi, you can manually edit:
# ~/.config/claude-code/mcp.json

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "mcp-server-github",
      "args": [],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "ghp_your_token_here"
      }
    }
  }
}

# Or use the CLI command with token as argument:
claude mcp add --transport stdio github --scope user -- mcp-server-github --token={{ .github_token }}

# Alternative: Set environment variable first, then add
export GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN={{ .github_token }}
claude mcp add --transport stdio github --scope user -- mcp-server-github
